    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2940",
      "problem": "A cinema has a rectangular hall whose dimensions are shown in the figure below. What is the area of the hall?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/e7263eb3d75ecb243301c2d6c5712dd77232b97b6839123febec3260b389b2e6.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a \\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na = 4.5\\,\\mathrm{m}, \\qquad b = 6\\,\\mathrm{m}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the area of the hall is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=4.5\\cdot 6=27\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
